            <ArticleTitle>Snapshots in surgery: small bowel intussusception following ileojejunal bypass.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>338-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccr3.132</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="KEY CLINICAL MESSAGE" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">Jejunal intussusception is a known complication of ileojejunal bypass surgery for obesity that may present as an acute abdomen. It can be avoided if the jejunum is anchored to the transverse mesocolon intra-operatively.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
